  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving lives of vulnerable populations through the provision of critical shelter and water, sanitation and hygiene assistance in underservedareas of Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As per the Humanitarian Needs and Response Plan (HNRP) for 2025, over 18,400 families affected by floods in Afghanistan remain in tents or damaged homes due to limited resources for repairs. With this funding envelope and in line with HNRP, IOM is prioritizing shelter repair solutions to disaster-affected populations as well as the rehabilitation and construction of water sources damaged by natural hazard-induced disasters during 2024&#x2013;2025 in underserved areas, aiming to enhance access to clean and safe water for drinking, sanitation, and hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
